# Repair recursive configuration overlays

The repository in `/workspace/repo` contains the `telemetry-config` Python library. Its public tests expose a regression in `merge_layers`: nested configuration overlays are applied as shallow replacements.

Fix the implementation so it obeys the documented contract in `telemetry/merge.py`:

- recursively merge mapping values;
- treat non-mapping values, including lists, as atomic replacements;
- remove a key when an overlay value is exactly the public `DELETE` sentinel;
- do not mutate or alias caller-owned base or overlay data.

Work only in `/workspace/repo`. Preserve the public API and make the complete test suite pass. You may add tests, but do not weaken or remove existing ones.

